---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';
// Full submission guide, rebuilt from the legacy ebneo.org/author-instructions/ page so the
// original URL keeps working (the /authors page links here; nav still points to /authors).
---
<Base title="Author Instructions"
      description="How to write and submit an EBNEO commentary: format, review headings, and the submission process through Acta Paediatrica.">
  <section class="panel">
    <p class="breadcrumb"><a href="/authors/">← For Authors</a></p>
    <article class="article">
      <h1>Author Instructions</h1>

      <h2>EBNEO background</h2>
      <p>Members of the International Society for Evidence-based Neonatology share a vision that all
        neonatal care should be firmly built on the best available evidence. The vision includes as
        short a passage from research-based knowledge to implementation in neonatal care
        (translation), thereby improving survival, decreasing morbidities, and promoting
        long-lasting health for newborn infants.</p>
      <p>The overall goals are:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>to provide an international forum to communicate and support evidence-based medicine for
          neonatal care in a global context;</li>
        <li>to provide an interactive forum for the critical evaluation of the literature;</li>
        <li>to provide neonatal care-givers with the best available knowledge by increasing the
          dissemination of evidence-based neonatology;</li>
        <li>to facilitate research projects on diagnostic procedures and interventions for important
          clinical outcomes.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>EBNEO commentaries</h2>
      <p>In keeping with our goals, in collaboration with and supported by
        <a href="http://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/journal/10.1111/(ISSN)1651-2227" rel="noopener">Acta
        Paediatrica</a>, EBNEO publishes monthly, concise, user-friendly, and peer-reviewed
        summaries of the best original articles related to the clinical care of neonates. These
        summaries provide readers with a structured abstract of the primary literature, along with a
        brief commentary focusing on the clinical implications of the study reviewed. The commentary
        is published in Acta Paediatrica, while the structured abstract is available here on
        EBNEO.org.</p>
      <p>EBNEO welcomes submissions of summaries of relevant clinical articles formatted as described
        below. The submission should include a cover letter with a brief description of why the
        article was chosen, as well as a list of authors and their contributions. Submissions follow
        the standardized format presented below and are reviewed by the section editor and sent for
        peer review.</p>

      <h2>Contact EBNEO before submission</h2>
      <p>To be certain that a commentary on a specific research paper has not already been submitted,
        please email <a href="mailto:clydejwright@mac.com">Clyde Wright</a> and confirm that a
        commentary would be considered before you start writing.</p>

      <h2>How to submit</h2>
      <p>All submissions are processed through the electronic manuscript system at
        <a href="https://wiley.atyponrex.com/journal/apa" rel="noopener">Acta Paediatrica</a>.</p>
      <p>Please note that the electronic submission process includes some required steps that are not
        applicable to our workflow. For example, your submission will be halted unless you enter a
        “running title” and an “abstract”. Where suitable, please type <em>not applicable.</em></p>

      <h2>Title page</h2>
      <p>The document that you upload needs to include a title page with:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>names, titles, and affiliations of authors;</li>
        <li>name and contact information for the corresponding author;</li>
        <li>funding (if any);</li>
        <li>conflicts of interest (if any).</li>
      </ul>
      <p><a class="btn" href="/documents/template.dot"><Icon name="file" /> Download the MS Word
        template</a></p>

      <h2>Review format</h2>
      <p>EBNEO reviews follow a specific format with the headings below: a structured abstract
        followed by the author’s commentary. The commentary is limited to <strong>500 words and 9
        references</strong>. Please note that only the commentary may include references.</p>
      <p>The full review is published on this website (ebneo.org); the commentary is also published
        in Acta Paediatrica with its own citable DOI.</p>
      <p><strong>References.</strong> Number the references consecutively in the order in which they
        are first mentioned in the text. Identify references by Arabic numerals (in parentheses).
        Observe the punctuation carefully. When there are more than six authors, list the first six
        and add “et al.” Examples:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><em>Kühl C, Andersen GE, Hertel J, Mölsted-Pedersen L. Metabolic events in infants of
          diabetic mothers during the first 24 hours after birth. Acta Paediatr 1982; 71:19-25.</em></li>
        <li><em>Stevenson DK, Fanaroff AA, Maisels MJ, Young BW, Wong RJ, Vreman HJ, et al.
          Prediction of hyperbilirubinemia in near-term and term infants. Pediatrics 2001;
          108:31–9.</em></li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Review headings</h2>
      <p>Structure the write-up using the following headings:</p>
      <dl class="headings">
        <dt>Title of write-up</dt>

        <dt>Manuscript citation</dt>
        <dd>Please use this format: <em>Manley BJ, Owen LS, Doyle LW, Andersen CC, Cartwright DW,
          Pritchard MA, Donath SM, Davis PG. High-Flow Nasal Cannulae in Very Preterm Infants after
          Extubation. N Engl J Med 2013; 369:1425-33. PMID 24106935.</em></dd>

        <dt>Reviewed by</dt>
        <dd>Name · Title · Institution · Email</dd>

        <dt>Type of investigation</dt>
        <dd>Choose one: prevention, treatment, diagnosis, prognosis, etiology, quality improvement or
          continuing medical education, economics of healthcare or interventions, clinical prediction
          guides, differential diagnosis, or systematic review.</dd>

        <dt>Question</dt>
        <dd>The question asked in the study, please state in the form of PICOT if appropriate
          (especially for an RCT).</dd>

        <dt>Methods</dt>
        <dd>
          <ul>
            <li>Design</li>
            <li>Allocation (see the <a href="https://acpjc.acponline.org/shared/glossary.htm" rel="noopener">ACP
              glossary</a>)</li>
            <li>Blinding (see the ACP glossary)</li>
            <li>Follow-up period</li>
            <li>Setting</li>
            <li>Patients, also include inclusion/exclusion criteria</li>
            <li>Intervention</li>
            <li>Outcomes</li>
            <li>Primary outcome</li>
            <li>Secondary outcomes</li>
            <li>Analysis and sample size</li>
            <li>Patient follow-up: % included in analysis</li>
          </ul>
        </dd>

        <dt>Main results</dt>
        <dd>Consider including demographics and details of interest to the reader. Main results may be
          presented as a table.</dd>

        <dt>Conclusion</dt>

        <dt>Commentary</dt>
        <dd>Limited to 500 words.</dd>

        <dt>References</dt>
        <dd>Only for the Commentary section and limited to 9. Number them consecutively in the order
          first mentioned; identify by Arabic numerals in parentheses; when there are more than six
          authors, list the first six and add “et al.”</dd>
      </dl>

      <p style="margin-top:32px">
        <a class="btn" href="/documents/template.dot"><Icon name="file" /> Download the MS Word
        template</a>
      </p>
    </article>
  </section>

  <style>
    .headings { margin: 8px 0 0; }
    .headings dt {
      font-weight: 700; color: var(--ink); text-transform: uppercase;
      letter-spacing: .04em; font-size: .9rem; margin-top: 20px;
    }
    .headings dd { margin: 4px 0 0; color: var(--ink-soft); }
    .headings dd ul { margin: 6px 0 0; }
  </style>
</Base>
